do_2 = "Create the minimal native object catalog, placement incarnation, upload-session, direct-child reservation and routing interfaces needed by the object service; allocate a free migration sequence during preflight. Keep logical object identity separate from physical S3 placement and legacy OIDs, and expose a real registered put/read/inspect consumer used by the case driver."
do_3 = "Implement conditional immutable uploads, multipart tracking, streaming digest/length/type verification and idempotent reconciliation against the selected S3 backend. Persist upload/verification outcomes outside long metadata transactions; conflicting bytes, incomplete parts, lost PUT responses and backend UNKNOWN outcomes must prevent false revision readiness."
do_4 = "Verify new tree closure inductively using direct-child protection receipts, including cross-owner reservations that remain protective after unknown parent outcomes. Update a fixed small change set inside increasing tree/directory fixtures and assert object/node work is bounded by affected paths rather than full-tree serialization."
do_5 = "1_1.py runs the real service/object catalog and codec paths, records backend identity and separately labels deterministic backend-fault cases and an actual S3 integration result. Assert independent reads reconstruct the exact pinned files without checkout, bucket LIST, Git invocation or native packs; do not represent a skipped live backend as PASS."
